# Git line-ending policy.
#
# We develop on Windows (autocrlf=true) but build Docker images on
# Linux. Shell scripts with CRLF line endings break dash/bash in the
# container with "'\r': command not found" or similar. Pin shell
# scripts to LF so the build doesn't depend on autocrlf at clone time.
#
# Pin Dockerfile line endings too — multi-stage Dockerfile ARG/ENV
# continuation can break if Windows rewrites them.
#
# Everything else follows Git's autocrlf default.

*.sh          text eol=lf
Dockerfile*   text eol=lf
*.dockerfile  text eol=lf
